<title>SPAIN: Montoro reaffirms Spain's strong EMU candidacy.</title>
<headline>Montoro reaffirms Spain's strong EMU candidacy.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish Economy Secretary Cristobal Montoro reiterated on Wednesday that Spain is one of the strongest candidates for entry into monetary union in 1999.</p>
<p>Speaking in an interview on national radio, Montoro said, &quot;In the last year we have made great progress and today Spain already fulfils three of the criteria (for monetary union) and therefore we are considered one of the firmest candidates to constitute monetary union.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
</text>
